# Owns the one list of installer-managed tools this fleet runs. install-tools.sh installs every row
# that names an npm package; doctor.sh checks every row. Adding or swapping a tool is one line here
# and a re-run of both - no rebuild, because none of this is in the Nix packing. The base packages
# are: they stay plain names in hosts/wsl-ubuntu.nix or hosts/mac.nix.
#
# A tool with its own installer keeps its step in install-tools.sh - a step is a paragraph of
# reasons, not a name - and names itself here only so the doctor knows to check it.
#
# Four whitespace-separated columns, '-' where a column does not apply:
#   tool     the executable's name, which is what the doctor looks for
#   npm      the npm package that provides it; '-' for its own installer, or for Nix's packing
#   check    run  = execute `<tool> --version`, because a stale shim of the right name resolves
#                  under `command -v` and then fails to exec
#            path = `command -v` is enough
#            -    = installed but not asserted
#   pane     pane = a live Herdr pane's environment must resolve it, else an agent cannot call it
#
# tool                npm                                check  pane
claude                -                                  run    pane
codex                 @openai/codex                      run    -
# `pi` must be named in full: plain `pi` on npm is an unrelated package about the digits of pi that
# installs a `pi` binary anyway, so every check below would pass on the wrong tool.
pi                    @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent    run    -
cursor-agent          -                                  run    -
grok                  -                                  run    -
no-mistakes           -                                  run    pane
treehouse             -                                  path   pane
gh-axi                gh-axi                             path   pane
tasks-axi             tasks-axi                          path   pane
lavish-axi            lavish-axi                         path   pane
chrome-devtools-axi   chrome-devtools-axi                path   pane
quota-axi             quota-axi                          path   pane
gnhf                  gnhf                               path   -
# Not asserted, so its install is allowed to fail on its own without failing the batch beside it.
backpass              backpass                           -      -
node                  -                                  path   -
npx                   -                                  path   -
gh                    -                                  path   -
gcloud                -                                  path   -
bq                    -                                  path   -
